From 48022af1a7f9bb3eec9be1324a140f29bb503a61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Bryniarski <michael.bryniarski@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:01:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dndcp: add native Wayland copy/paste

On a Wayland session vmware-user uses the X11 clipboard through
Xwayland, which depends on the compositor syncing the Wayland clipboard
to X11. KWin only does that while an X11 window has focus, which
vmware-user never has, so guest-to-host copy fails.

CopyPasteUIWayland uses a data control protocol instead, which reads and
sets the clipboard without a window: ext-data-control-v1, or its
predecessor wlr-data-control-unstable-v1 where a compositor only has
that.

- Host to guest: the host's text and RTF, PNG image or file list becomes
  a data control source set as the selection. Files are offered from a
  vmblock-blocked staging directory, and a monitor thread requests the
  transfer on first access. The staging directory is passed to
  SrcUIRequestFiles; with none, the common layer creates a second
  directory the files would land in. A file list with any unsafe name is
  refused (see WaylandUtil_IsSafeRelativePath).
- Guest to host: selection events track the current clipboard and
  whether another client set it. On the host's request its file list, or
  PNG, RTF and text, are read without blocking and sent, or "not changed"
  if nothing new was copied since the last time.

CopyPasteDnDX11 holds the copy/paste UI through a CopyPasteUI interface
and uses CopyPasteUIWayland when the compositor offers either data
control protocol, and CopyPasteUIX11 otherwise (e.g. GNOME).
VMTOOLS_CP_BACKEND=x11|wayland forces either. Only the regular clipboard
is synced, not the primary selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
